#6212 is in the merge queue. the user who reported "factory samples go silent after relaunch" wants a reply; I mostly need a short plain-language explanation of what was wrong and what changed. sanity check the lane's summary first so I don't promise something that isn't true. files are in the working dir.

lane summary:

> 1. On later launches `seedFactoryLibrary` marks the restored factory root ready instead of leaving it offline; first launch still renders, caches and persists once.
> 2. A disconnected factory root stays gone: the seed flag means "seeded once", so a set flag with no root is never recreated.
> 3. `ensureFactorySampleBuffer` resolves in order: resident cache entry, PCM stored this or an earlier launch (`restoreUnpinnedAudioBuffersFromIdb`, which pins nothing), then one render of the pack.
> 4. Concurrent callers share one render (`renderFactoryLibraryPack` memoises the in-flight promise).
> 5. A render is cached (and so stored) only when storage holds nothing for that sample; when storage can't be read the sample plays this session via `holdAudioBufferForSession` and is never written.
> 6. Rescan re-renders and caches only samples with no stored audio.
> 7. Glitch Stutter uses a seeded LCG, so the pack renders identically every time.
> 8. Every reader of a factory sample's buffer now goes through `ensureFactorySampleBuffer` — Library preview and timeline drop were the two; the other cache reads are clip-buffer reads in the renderers, not library reads:
