PR body:

fix(library): obtain factory sample buffers on demand instead of at launch (#6212)

Factory samples stopped playing after a relaunch: the factory root is
synthesised, so restoring the library brought it back offline with no
buffers, and preview said the audio buffer was not available. The
factory root now comes back ready, and every reader of a factory
sample's buffer (preview, timeline drop) obtains it on demand: the
resident cache entry, then PCM stored this session, then one render of
the pack shared by concurrent callers. Rescan re-renders the pack. The
Glitch Stutter generator now uses a seeded random source, so the pack
renders identically each time and saved clips keep matching audio.
